<https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/catalog#linkset/sdtm-model_code_variable_to_its_long_version>
    a void:Linkset ;
    dcterms:accessRights "Built locally, not published: it starts from or ends at a sign-in source." ;
    dcterms:description "An SDTM Model variable row whose name ends in \"CD\" to the Model row of the variable it is the short version of, in the same class and dataset." ;
    dcterms:title "sdtm-model code variable to its long version" ;
    dcterms:type "by rule" ;
    void:linkPredicate <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/rule/sdtm-model/SDTM#Variable%20Name/sdtm-model/SDTM> ;
    void:objectsTarget <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/graph/sdtm-model> ;
    void:subjectsTarget <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/graph/sdtm-model> ;
    rdfs:comment "Rule: SDTMIG v3.4, 4.2.1: variables with names ending in \"CD\" are short versions of the associated variables without the \"CD\" suffix (e.g. --TESTCD is the short version of --TEST). Only for a Variable Name ending in \"CD\": the Model row with the same Class and Dataset Name (both empty for a variable the Model publishes for a class) whose Variable Name is the name without the final \"CD\"." ;
.

<https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/catalog#linkset/sdtm-model_variable_name_as_fragment>
    a void:Linkset ;
    dcterms:accessRights "Built locally, not published: it starts from or ends at a sign-in source." ;
    dcterms:description "An SDTM Model variable row whose name, without a leading \"--\", is a variable-naming fragment of SDTMIG Appendix D, to that fragment row." ;
    dcterms:title "sdtm-model variable name as fragment" ;
    dcterms:type "by rule" ;
    void:linkPredicate <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/rule/sdtm-model/SDTM#Variable%20Name/sdtmig-fragments/CDISC%20Variable-naming%20Fragments> ;
    void:objectsTarget <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/graph/sdtmig-fragments> ;
    void:subjectsTarget <https://kerfors.github.io/cdisc-for-all/graph/sdtm-model> ;
    rdfs:comment "Rule: The Variable Name with a leading \"--\" removed equals a Fragment as published (a Fragment cell that lists more than one, such as \"ST, STD\", split at \",\", surrounding spaces removed). Every matching fragment row is linked; a name that matches more than one row (the same fragment for more than one keyword) is reported." ;
.

